# TRACE v0.2.0

Major MVP Refinement Update

"Every Task Leaves a Trace."

## Overview

TRACE v0.2.0 focuses on refining the core user experience, improving task organization, enhancing accountability workflows, and making the application feel more polished, interactive, and production-ready.

This update improves nearly every major area of the application while preserving TRACE's core philosophy:

Every task leaves a permanent record of its journey and outcome.

---

## Highlights

### Activity Journal Redesign

The Activity page has been completely redesigned into an Operational Journal.

Instead of functioning as a dashboard, Activity now answers:

* What happened?
* What is happening?
* What will happen next?

New structure:

* Today's Summary
* Activity Timeline
* Upcoming Transitions

Timeline entries include:

✓ Completed
✕ Failed
→ Became Active
⟳ Reattempted

History is grouped into:

* Today
* Yesterday
* Past Week
* Past Month

---

## Improved Tags & Projects

Tags are now functional.

Users can:

* Create tags
* Search by tags
* Filter by tags

Projects have been upgraded with new default categories:

* Personal
* College
* Work
* Health

Users can also create custom project categories for better task organization.

---

## Better Search

Search has been expanded to support:

* Task titles
* Descriptions
* Tags
* Projects

This makes task retrieval significantly faster and more practical as task history grows.

---

## Task History Improvements

Completed and Failed tasks now scale better over time.

Features include:

* Search
* Filtering
* Automatic monthly grouping

Examples:

* June 2026
* May 2026
* April 2026

This keeps historical task records accessible without overwhelming users.

---

## Reattempt Workflow

Failed tasks can now be reattempted more intelligently.

Selecting:

Reattempt Task

will:

* Open the task creation page
* Prefill existing information
* Allow full editing before creating a new task

The original failed task remains permanently preserved.

---

## Task Creation Improvements

The task creation experience has been refined.

Changes include:

* Cleaner page layout
* Improved placeholder text
* Better field hierarchy
* Simplified labels
* Improved start-time behavior

Start Time now properly works as:

Optional → Starts immediately if left empty

